/S /H1
/P 287 0 R
/T (CULTURAL ACTIVITIES University life shouldn't be limited to lectures and studying, but should also be a time for personal and collective growth. For this reason, we organize cultural activities, courses, and seminars, as well as recreational activities such as GulliveRock, now in its thirty-second year, as well as aperitifs and parties both inside and outside the University. All activities are inspired by ideas from students, both members and non-members, which Gulliver promotes. Gulliver's potential is enormous, and to fully exploit it, everyone's contribution is needed. If you'd like to contribute, stop by our Faculty Meeting Rooms, connect with us on our social media pages, or join our weekly meetings held every Tuesday at 9:30 PM.)
