383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (Also this year we find ourselves denouncing the increasingly critical situation affecting the Italian university system and, in particular, the Right to Education. Italy continues to follow a direction opposite to that which should characterize a country that recognizes education as one of the main tools for social and collective growth.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (Beyond the triumphalist narrative promoted by the Ministry, reality tells a very different picture, Italian universities continue to suffer the effects of a systematic defunding of the university system.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (The consequences on the Marche region are obvious, fewer resources translate into greater precariousness, a downsizing of services and an increasingly heated competition between universities to ensure survival. This consolidates a university model similar to a company, where the logic of performance prevails over the critical and formative function of knowledge. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (We students are the ones who suffer the effects, forced to deal with increasing pressure to achieve standards of "excellence" within increasingly rigid times.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (6)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 291 0 R
/T (The regional program on the Right to Education above all returns a sense of uncertainty: uncertainty about the possibility of continuing to guarantee access to economic benefits and scholarships to all those who are entitled to them. Despite the reassurances of the Council, which continues to declare its intention to ensure coverage for all eligible people, the body for the right to study continues to affirm that it has strong doubts about the actual availability of resources and the sustainability of the commitments made.)
/E (The regional program on the Right to Education above all returns a sense of uncertainty: uncertainty about the possibility of continuing to guarantee access to economic benefits and scholarships to all those who are entitled to them. Despite the reassurances of the Council, which continues to declare its intention to ensure coverage for all eligible people, the body for the right to study continues to affirm that it has strong doubts about the actual availability of resources and the sustainability of the commitments made.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 291 0 R
/T (Added to this is an increasingly serious housing crisis, which for years has been one of the main obstacles to effective access to the Right to Education. Public beds continue to be largely insufficient while the cost of rents on the private market reaches increasingly unsustainable figures. The interventions carried out so far through PNRR funds have proven insufficient and, in many cases, unable to concretely resolve a structural problem affecting Ancona.)
/E (Added to this is an increasingly serious housing crisis, which for years has been one of the main obstacles to effective access to the Right to Education. Public beds continue to be largely insufficient while the cost of rents on the private market reaches increasingly unsustainable figures. The interventions carried out so far through PNRR funds have proven insufficient and, in many cases, unable to concretely resolve a structural problem affecting Ancona.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 291 0 R
/T ( In fact, it was decided to entrust a significant part of the interventions to private entities, fueling a model that ends up transforming a fundamental right into an opportunity for profit. It is unacceptable that private operators continue to be allowed to profit from the pockets of the student, without addressing the structural causes.)
/E ( In fact, it was decided to entrust a significant part of the interventions to private entities, fueling a model that ends up transforming a fundamental right into an opportunity for profit. It is unacceptable that private operators continue to be allowed to profit from the pockets of the student, without addressing the structural causes.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
