393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 292 0 R
/T (Added to this are the difficulties encountered by international students, attracted by ambitious enrolment campaigns that result in empty shop windows. Too often they find themselves excluded from calls for scholarships due to slow bureaucracy, documentation that is very difficult to find, and discriminatory rules that hinder their right to study in decent conditions.)
/E (Added to this are the difficulties encountered by international students, attracted by ambitious enrolment campaigns that result in empty shop windows. Too often they find themselves excluded from calls for scholarships due to slow bureaucracy, documentation that is very difficult to find, and discriminatory rules that hinder their right to study in decent conditions.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 292 0 R
/T (To further worsen this already dramatic picture, there is the reform of the filter semester, presented as an opening and a sign of inclusion, but which has turned out, in reality, in yet another hypocritical and purely propagandistic measure. The limited number, in fact, has not been abolished, but simply postponed, turning into a deferred selection that has worsened the condition of thousands of students.)
/E (To further worsen this already dramatic picture, there is the reform of the filter semester, presented as an opening and a sign of inclusion, but which has turned out, in reality, in yet another hypocritical and purely propagandistic measure. The limited number, in fact, has not been abolished, but simply postponed, turning into a deferred selection that has worsened the condition of thousands of students.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (8)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 293 0 R
/T (The access model has been built on a prolonged selective system, which increases uncertainty and unloads the entire responsibility for "merit" on the shoulders of the student, without however offering any real guarantee of inclusion or support. This change feeds the illusion of free access for all, while in reality it reinforces social inequalities and further precarious educational paths, transforming the university into an obstacle course that selects on the basis of economic possibilities.)
/E (The access model has been built on a prolonged selective system, which increases uncertainty and unloads the entire responsibility for "merit" on the shoulders of the student, without however offering any real guarantee of inclusion or support. This change feeds the illusion of free access for all, while in reality it reinforces social inequalities and further precarious educational paths, transforming the university into an obstacle course that selects on the basis of economic possibilities.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 293 0 R
/T (As a student union, we cannot remain silent in the face of this drift. We will continue to mobilize and claim a truly public, free and accessible University, which does not select by "merit", which does not force anyone to abandon their studies for economic reasons, and which does not transform the student into a commodity to be evaluated on the basis of market logic.)
/E (As a student union, we cannot remain silent in the face of this drift. We will continue to mobilize and claim a truly public, free and accessible University, which does not select by "merit", which does not force anyone to abandon their studies for economic reasons, and which does not transform the student into a commodity to be evaluated on the basis of market logic.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
