/P 348 0 R
/T (If I change courses, do I have to return the scholarship? Will I be able to get it back in the future? It depends. If you transfer to a different degree program, you will not be required to return the scholarship you received, for the reasons previously explained. However, you would be required to return the scholarship if you withdrew from your first-year program and subsequently applied for benefits for the first year of a new program \(effectively resetting your academic record\).)
/E (If I change courses, do I have to return the scholarship? Will I be able to get it back in the future? It depends. If you transfer to a different degree program, you will not be required to return the scholarship you received, for the reasons previously explained. However, you would be required to return the scholarship if you withdrew from your first-year program and subsequently applied for benefits for the first year of a new program \(effectively resetting your academic record\).)
/Pg 73 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
