/Title (The regional program on the Right to Education above all returns a sense of uncertainty: uncertainty about the possibility of continuing to guarantee access to economic benefits and scholarships to all those who are entitled to them. Despite the reassurances of the Council, which continues to declare its intention to ensure coverage for all eligible people, the body for the right to study continues to affirm that it has strong doubts about the actual availability of resources and the sustainability of the commitments made.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2689 0 R
/Next 2737 0 R
>>
endobj
2736 0 obj
<<
/Title (If I change courses, do I have to return the scholarship? Will I be able to get it back in the future? It depends. If you transfer to a different degree program, you will not be required to return the scholarship you received, for the reasons previously explained. However, you would be required to return the scholarship if you withdrew from your first-year program and subsequently applied for benefits for the first year of a new program \(effectively resetting your academic record\).)
/Dest [73 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2738 0 R
/Next 2690 0 R
>>
endobj
2737 0 obj
<<
/Title (Added to this is an increasingly serious housing crisis, which for years has been one of the main obstacles to effective access to the Right to Education. Public beds continue to be largely insufficient while the cost of rents on the private market reaches increasingly unsustainable figures. The interventions carried out so far through PNRR funds have proven insufficient and, in many cases, unable to concretely resolve a structural problem affecting Ancona.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2735 0 R
/Next 2739 0 R
>>
