/Title (The access model has been built on a prolonged selective system, which increases uncertainty and unloads the entire responsibility for "merit" on the shoulders of the student, without however offering any real guarantee of inclusion or support. This change feeds the illusion of free access for all, while in reality it reinforces social inequalities and further precarious educational paths, transforming the university into an obstacle course that selects on the basis of economic possibilities.)
